From 8f6d5df32fcba961cc07ffb39e8d39d466671a39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aignis <6974796+aignis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 10:27:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] diagnostics: renderer captures by swap count, scripted
 pad input; desktop env overrides

NativeRenderer captures capture_<n>.bmp at the swap counts in
CTR_NATIVE_CAPTURE_SWAPS (or capture_swaps in Switch 2's ctr-native.ini),
without SDL surfaces so it works on the console. Internal builds read
CTR_NATIVE_AUTOPAD to hold pad bits during given input updates.
CTR_NATIVE_VOICES/WIDESCREEN/UNLOCK_ALL set the ctr-web options on desktop.
Used to check the LP64 build with ctr-web's PAL data on Apple Silicon: main
menu, Spanish text, widescreen and a time trial race render correctly.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 include/platform/native_renderer.h |   1 +
 main.c                             |  31 ++++++++-
 platform/native_input.c            |  47 +++++++++++++
 platform/native_renderer.c         | 105 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 182 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

